From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Berkay=20K=C3=B6sebay?= <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 23:28:38 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] drm/imagination: apple: Boot the A9 (S8003) GPU firmware

The iPad 5's GPU is a Rogue GT7600 whose firmware, Apple's, runs on the
core's own META processor. The powervr driver now takes the A9's node
(apple,s8003-gpu) next to the A10's and starts that firmware:

- It unpacks the device's own firmware file, a META LDR image, with the
  driver's LDR walker into the block Apple's bootloader expects, and adds
  the bootloader's configuration.
- The firmware's page tables are the kernel VM context's: the image, its
  root and shared memory and the registers it uses are mapped there, at
  the firmware's addresses. The bus addresses of those registers (Fender,
  the Rogue core, the interrupt controller) and the number of its
  interrupt come from the device tree.
- The registers of a META boot go into Fender's boot stream; the core is
  powered up through Fender, and the driver waits for the firmware's
  "alive" event, then gives it an empty device-control command and waits
  until the firmware took it.
- Stopping is Fender's power state 0; runtime PM stops the firmware a
  second after its last use and starts it again from the kept image, as
  on the A10.

One boot path: Apple's unmodified image, the governor pinned to the
state the core is powered up in (the fastest, 4, unless the
apple_perf_state parameter names another).

The firmware's commands are not written yet, so no context can be
created and nothing renders. The core counts as experimental: the driver
binds only with powervr.exp_hw_support=1. Without it the probe wakes
Fender, reads the core's ID and powers the GPU off again.

The firmware's interrupt to the host is not taken; the driver reads the
firmware's rings on a timer while it runs.

[Orchard: ported from orchard PR #74 (apple-g5p boot.inc, boot-layout.h,
pack.h, fender.h, perf-envelope.h, lifecycle.inc), reshaped as a chip of
the powervr driver's Apple firmware path. Not ported: see
docs/bring-up/gpu/a9-g5p.md in orchard.]

Assisted-by: LLM
